    "policy": {
      "purpose": "capability_retention_of_a_constructed_or_trained_arm_against_the_frozen_source",
      "rationale": "G1_QUALITY closed the token-salad hole at initialization, but every check it applies is likelihood- or teacher-agreement-shaped, and those are now measured to decouple from capability. At a token-matched 500,099-target dose a CED arm reached held-out CE 0.4727 against the frozen source's 5.5782 -- 5.1055 nats BETTER than its own teacher -- while answering 2 of 60 held-out questions the source answers 20 of 60, with disjoint 95% intervals. Of the eight non-task signals the run records, seven admit no separating threshold and four invert; the eighth, top-1 agreement with the source, separates by only 0.0038 (0.32798 vs 0.32416) against a registered G1_QUALITY floor of 0.5 that both arms fail, and it is still closing. So none supports a defensible registered threshold. This stage scores answers instead. Corrected after SIGNAL_SEPARATION.json falsified the stronger claim originally written here, which was that no likelihood-shaped quantity separates the two models at all -- the same shape of overstatement HOTFIX-004 had to retract from HOTFIX-003.",
      "threshold_provenance": "Transcribed unchanged from RETENTION_GATE_DESIGN.md, committed at f7bc290 before this code existed and before any arm was scored under the typed grammar. The rules are policy tolerances, not values fitted to an arm. max_correct_to_incorrect_per_class is 0 because a gate that permits any forgetting has to justify the permitted amount, and no measurement here supports a number; min_termination_rate_per_class REUSES the existing G0.min_termination_rate of 0.8 rather than inventing a value; min_source_correct_terminated_per_class is 1, the weakest statement that rules out the arithmetic_chain failure where the teacher scores 0 and the probe measures nothing. Historical arm scores under the LEGACY number-sequence scorer were already known when these rules were written, so applying them to an already-measured arm is retrospective demonstration, never preregistered validation. Source scores under this grammar were not known.",
      "scored_split": "monitor_probe",
      "probe_classes": [
        "percentage_reasoning",
        "ratio_proportion",
        "time_duration"
      ],
      "excluded_probe_class": "arithmetic_chain",
      "excluded_probe_class_reason": "the frozen source scores 0/20, so every arm would read 0/N before and after and the probe would measure nothing",
      "reference_rule": "union_of_frozen_source_correct_and_arm_initialization_correct",
      "max_correct_to_incorrect_per_class": 0,
      "min_source_correct_terminated_per_class": 1,
      "confirmation_min_retention_is_inert": "The separately designed confirmation certificate pairs an exact binomial bound of 0.10 with a 9/10 retention floor. The floor can never bind: for alpha=1/180 the Clopper-Pearson upper limit always exceeds k/m, so bound<=0.10 already implies retention>0.9 (verified exhaustively for m<=600). Worse, at the registered minimum m=50 only ZERO losses clear the bound -- one loss does not clear it until m=70 -- so the certificate demands 100% retention at its own minimum panel size, not 90%. Recorded, not silently repaired: the confirmation lane is not implemented or licensed.",
      "min_termination_rate_per_class": 0.8,
